# Which infectious disease kills the most people today?
subtitle: "Tap the infection you think kills the most people today, then hear why an old, curable disease is still on top, ahead of COVID, HIV and malaria."
tags: ["health","epidemiology","data"]
format: quiz
thumb: "band \"Not the one you think\" note \"1 germ, 1 million deaths\""

## Which infectious disease kills the most people today?
use: bar_chart
with:
    labels:
      - Malaria
      - HIV/AIDS
      - COVID-19
      - TB
      - Pneumonia
    values:
      - 670
      - 830
      - 850
      - 1010
      - 2500
    value_labels: true
    ylim:
      - 0
      - 2800
    y_label: Deaths in 2023 (thousands)
    box: full
    bar_colors: same
    label_size: 30
    icons:
      - {of: mosquito, set: twemoji}
      - {of: reminder ribbon, set: twemoji}
      - {of: face with medical mask, set: twemoji}
      - {of: lungs, set: twemoji}
      - {of: face with thermometer, set: twemoji}
sources:
    - id: owid
      title: Number of deaths from tuberculosis
      authors: Our World in Data, from IHME Global Burden of Disease (2025)
      year: 2025
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/tuberculosis-deaths
      finding: about 1.01 million tuberculosis deaths in 2023
    - id: owid_causes
      title: Annual number of deaths by cause
      authors: Our World in Data, from IHME Global Burden of Disease (2025)
      year: 2025
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/annual-number-of-deaths-by-cause
      finding: 'IHME estimates for 2023: tuberculosis 1.01 million, COVID-19 847,000, HIV/AIDS 833,000, malaria 670,000, lower respiratory infections (pneumonia) 2.5 million; COVID-19 exceeded tuberculosis in 2020–2022. WHO''s own estimates differ (TB about 1.25 million, HIV about 630,000, malaria about 597,000) but also put TB first among single infectious agents'
    - id: owid_tb
      title: Tuberculosis; Once a leading killer, tuberculosis is now rare in rich countries
      authors: Saloni Dattani, Fiona Spooner, Hannah Ritchie and Max Roser (Our World in Data)
      year: 2025
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/tuberculosis-history-decline
      finding: as much as one quarter of deaths in Europe and the US were once from tuberculosis; streptomycin, the first antibiotic against it, was found in 1944; treatment takes months

    icon ic_mal size 180 set twemoji x 140 y 450 icon_look picture of mosquito hidden true
    icon ic_hiv size 180 set twemoji x 370 y 450 or ["reminder ribbon","ribbon"] icon_look picture of "red ribbon" hidden true
    icon ic_cov size 180 set twemoji x 600 y 450 icon_look picture of "face with medical mask" hidden true
    icon ic_tb size 180 set twemoji x 840 y 450 icon_look picture of lungs hidden true
    text l_mal "Malaria" x 140 y 300 font_size 44 hidden true
    text l_hiv "HIV/AIDS" x 370 y 300 font_size 44 hidden true
    text l_cov "COVID-19" x 600 y 300 font_size 44 hidden true
    text l_tb "Tuberculosis" x 840 y 300 font_size 44 hidden true
    text old "1800s: up to 1 in 4 deaths" #2f6b8f cites ["owid_tb"] x 420 y 560 font_size 44 hidden true
    text many "many germs" #2f2b26 at.ref bar_5 cites ["owid_causes"] font_size 34 hidden true

    card title "Which infection kills the most?"

A: Which single infectious disease kills the most people in the world today? Here are four candidates.
    draw ic_mal l_mal ic_hiv l_hiv ic_cov l_cov ic_tb l_tb

B: Easy. COVID. Everyone I know has had it.
    highlight ic_cov

    ask "Tap the one you think kills the most." choose ["ic_mal","ic_hiv","ic_cov","ic_tb"] answer ic_tb default ic_cov reveal.text "No. 1" reveal.at.x 840 reveal.at.y 620 reveal.size 48
        right: Tuberculosis: about a million deaths in 2023 by one major estimate, more than any other single germ.
        wrong: Think of a disease many people believe belongs to the past.

    erase ic_mal l_mal ic_hiv l_hiv ic_cov l_cov ic_tb l_tb

A: By one major estimate, in 2023 malaria killed about six hundred and seventy thousand people, HIV about eight hundred and thirty thousand, and COVID about eight hundred and fifty thousand.
    draw axes bar_1 bar_2 bar_3

A: And tuberculosis: about a million. Back on top, after COVID passed it for a few years.
    draw bar_4

B: Tuberculosis? Isn't that a disease from old novels?
    highlight bar_4

A: It was the great killer of the eighteen hundreds: once as many as one death in four in Europe and America.
    draw old

    erase old

B: Hang on. Doesn't pneumonia kill more?
    draw bar_5 many

A: It does, about two and a half million. But pneumonia is many different germs. Tuberculosis is one bacterium.
    highlight bar_5

    erase many

A: And here's the twist: it's curable. Antibiotics have cured it since the 1940s. But treatment takes months, and the poorest places often never get the diagnosis.
    text cure "CURABLE" above bar_4 gap 55 #b5482e cites ["owid_tb"] font_size 56
    text cue "cure exists, not delivered" #8f887c x 360 y 600 font_size 40

B: Wait. So we have the cure. We just don't get it to the people who need it?
    highlight cue

A: Exactly. The germ isn't winning. We are losing on delivery.
    highlight bar_4

## Thumbnail
role: thumbnail

    icon m size 210 set twemoji x 170 y 470 icon_look picture of mosquito hidden true
    icon v size 210 set twemoji x 390 y 470 icon_look picture of "face with medical mask" hidden true
    icon r size 210 set twemoji x 610 y 470 or ["reminder ribbon"] icon_look picture of "red ribbon" hidden true
    icon l size 210 set twemoji x 830 y 470 icon_look picture of lungs hidden true
    text q "Which kills most?" #2f2b26 x 500 y 300 font_size 80 hidden true
    thumb band "Not the one you think" kind band hidden true

## Thumbnail
role: thumbnail

    icon mic size 260 set twemoji x 200 y 430 icon_look picture of "studio microphone" hidden true
    text s1 "“COVID, obviously.”" #2f2b26 x 620 y 520 font_size 64 hidden true
    text s2 "“…nope.”" #b5482e x 680 y 380 font_size 80 hidden true
    thumb band "Wrong guess, live" kind band hidden true

## Thumbnail
role: thumbnail

    icon l size 330 set twemoji x 700 y 430 icon_look picture of microbe hidden true
    text a "1 germ." #2f2b26 x 260 y 460 font_size 90 hidden true
    text b "? deaths" #b5482e x 260 y 330 font_size 90 hidden true
    text c "a year" #8f887c x 260 y 230 font_size 60 hidden true
    thumb burst "Still?" kind burst hidden true
